  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field in a region is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The ratio of flux of reported field through the rectangular surface of area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> (parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;plane) to that of the surface of area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> (parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></math> plane) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>?</mo></math>&nbsp;[Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> are unit vectors along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> -axes respectively]",
